      "writtenOn": "2014-06-25T05:13:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is just no great cross-database solution here. Abstracting away the query seems like a way to help control divergent behavior in databases. It sounds like using window functions is a significant optimization for some databases that would be useful to pursue in subsequent patches.\n\nRegarding the time window, I do not think the target cut-off should change as the program runs. Otherwise the behavior would be non-deterministic given a known data-set. In this case, I think we want an admin to be able to predict what the tool will do. If it were to run too slowly for some reason, it might just run forever.",
      "parentUuid": "1ae5cdf2_6cbe70b0",
